					<description><![CDATA[Nonwoven geotextiles are synthetic fabrics commonly used in civil engineering and construction projects for a variety of applications. They are made from synthetic fibers that are bonded together through methods like needle punching, heat bonding, or chemical bonding, rather than being woven.

<hr />

